{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed from Mount Hor.</b> It returns to the earlier matter — how Israel turned away from the king of Edom — only that it interrupted in between with the death of Aaron and the war with Amalek that came upon them on account of the death of Aaron." "<b>From Mount Hor by way of the Sea of Reeds.</b> From north to south, to go around Edom. This circuit is not the same as the circuit of Mount Seir mentioned in the section of Devarim, ונסב את הר שעיר ימים רבים, for that was in the twenty-first year after their exodus from Egypt, after the nineteen years they dwelt in Kadesh Barnea from when the spies were sent, and they circled Mount Seir from Kadesh Barnea to Kadesh of the wilderness of Zin. But this circuit was in the fortieth year after their exodus from Egypt, when they came to Kadesh of the wilderness of Zin, at the edge of the border of the land of Edom. Because the king of Edom did not let them pass through, they turned back from Mount Hor from north to south and went out of the land of Edom from the part they had entered, and this is what is said: לסבוב את ארץ אדום, and they circled from there the entire southern side of the land of Moab, for they too did not let them pass, as it is written, וגם אל מלך מואב שלח ולא אבה. And when they reached Oboth, in the southeastern corner of the land of Moab, they turned their faces northward and skirted to their left along the entire eastern side, as far as the wadi Arnon, as it is written, וילך במדבר ויסב את ארץ אדום ואת ארץ מואב ויבאו מזרחה שמש לארץ מואב ויחנו בעבר ארנון. Here Rashi did not explain what HaShem warned Israel concerning Moab and Ammon, and he explained it in the section of Devarim. Also here he did not explain how many encampments they made from this point onward, and in the section of Masei are written Hor HaHar, Zalmonah, Punon, Oboth." "<b>And the people's spirit grew short on the way.</b> An expression of קוצר רוח — that is, their spirit and breath grew short because of the hardship of the circuit around the land of Edom, as Rashi explained: they were close to entering from south to north through the land of Edom, and they had to turn back from north to south the distance they had already entered. Another interpretation: ותקצר נפש העם בדרך — the sun beat down fiercely upon them, for the clouds of glory had departed from the time Aaron died."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "The text has פונון (Punon) where the biblical verse in Numbers 33:42 reads פונון; rendered as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:04.209985068Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}